        "original_id": "8a67c98c-4a03-58a9-8b42-b90d7b56a82f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sunye, Min Sun-ye, Stephen Pearcy, Sohee, Hyuna, Al Pitrelli, Hiro Kuretani\n- Groups: Wonder Girls, Vertex, Ratt, Arcade, Vicious Delite, Nitronic, Danger Danger, Hotshot, Alice Cooper, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, Trans-Siberian Orchestra, WXXI, Trancentral Station\n- Roles: missionary, singer, actress, musician, guitarist, drummer\n\nFacts:\n- Stephen Pearcy was born on July 3, 1956, and he is an American musician.\n- Sunye, whose birth name is Min Sun-ye, was born on August 12, 1989, and she is a South Korean missionary and a former singer and actress on hiatus.\n- Vertex was a band formed in 1995 featuring singer Stephen Pearcy, guitarist Al Pitrelli, and drummer Hiro Kuretani.\n- Stephen Pearcy was associated with Ratt, Arcade, Vicious Delite, and Nitronic in the Vertex description.\n- Al Pitrelli was associated with Danger Danger, Hotshot, Alice Cooper, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, and Trans-Siberian Orchestra in the Vertex description.\n- Hiro Kuretani was associated with WXXI and Trancentral Station in the Vertex description.\n- In late 2007, Hyuna left Wonder Girls.\n- In 2015, Sunye and Sohee officially left Wonder Girls.\n- Sunye was also known as Sunye or Sun, with SunYe as a stylized form.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
